package std.net

// The client-side target a `TcpListener` resource name gives where an
// `Endpoint` is expected (`docs/slice.md` 14.14 item 5), and the result
// of the substrate builtin `Endpoint.of`.
//
// `Endpoint.of(reference: Ref<K>) -> Result<Endpoint, IoError>` is a
// builtin static of this module, implemented in the substrate and not
// declared here (16.9, 16.13): it resolves a reference's path text through
// the process arguments `--ref <path>=<address>:<port>` that `ignite run`
// passes to a probe, and fails with "no binding for <path>" outside a
// run. The module is also the substrate's `TcpListener`, `TcpStream` and
// `Exposure`, and since slice 14 (18.3, 18.4) the interface `ByteStream`
// (implemented by `TcpStream`, `PipeStream` and a type parameter bounded
// by it), the test-only `Pipe.pair()` and its ends, `PipeStream`.
type Endpoint {
  address: Text
  port: Int
}
